How can new software engineers practice the skills needed to maintain production and fix production issues (without throwing them head-first into a SEV-1)? 

We've been iterating with the @resolveai team on a new assignment for our Stanford course 𝗧𝗵𝗲 𝗠𝗼𝗱𝗲𝗿𝗻 𝗦𝗼𝗳𝘁𝘄𝗮𝗿𝗲 𝗗𝗲𝘃𝗲𝗹𝗼𝗽𝗲𝗿. It might be the coolest and most practical homework exercise I've ever seen. 

@maynkag, Resolve CTO and founder, and Milind Ganjoo, technical lead, will be guest lecturing for the class tomorrow (𝟭𝟭/𝟮𝟭) 𝗮𝘁 𝟴:𝟯𝟬𝗮𝗺 𝗼𝗻 𝗦𝘁𝗮𝗻𝗳𝗼𝗿𝗱 𝗰𝗮𝗺𝗽𝘂𝘀 (𝗯𝘂𝗶𝗹𝗱𝗶𝗻𝗴 𝟰𝟮𝟬, 𝗿𝗼𝗼𝗺 𝟬𝟰𝟭). Join us!

